{"content":"## Thread 4 — fourth copy of the terminal-story boilerplate

Extracted in `lib/src/providers/transient_retry_stream.dart`:

- `_terminalStory(model, attemptLog, startedAt, story)` — the shared message shell (empty content, model identity, zero usage, error stop) used by `_zeroByteStallMessage` (gh-1308), `_exhausted` (issue #290 AC2), and `_rateLimitDeadlineTerminal` (gh-1602);
- `_storyLog(attemptLog)` / `_storyElapsed(startedAt)` — the shared evidence pieces (trailing-dot-stripped log join, `<1s` elapsed text), also reused by `_resumedExhaustion` (issue #1168), which keeps its own shell because the snapshot's content/usage/raw vendor verdict ride along.

Each terminal is now a single call site building only its headline sentence, so the next evidence-format change is single-touch. All four `errorMessage` outputs are byte-identical to before (the existing message-pinning tests pass unchanged).
