The full suite is still running (it pipes through `tail` so no output until done — ~10.7k tests). While waiting, let me run a few more targeted suites that touch the ladder indirectly (agent_loop tests already ran; connect stall, stale keepalive ran with test/providers). 

Let me also double-check one edge I changed: the `_pauseBetweenAttempts` watchdog path. In the OLD code:
```dart
if (survived) return true;
if (cancelToken?.cancelReason is RunIdleWatchdogFire) { cancelToken?.reset(); return true; }
_pushAborted(...); return false;
```
NEW:
```dart
if (!survived && cancelToken?.cancelReason is! RunIdleWatchdogFire) { _pushAborted(...); return false; }
transientRetryNotice?.call(...);
if (survived) return true;
cancelToken?.reset();
return true;
```

Equivalent except the notice on user-cancel is gone. ✓ (zero-byte watchdog tests passed — 1189 agent+provider tests.)

Also let me write the response.md draft now, and while the suite runs, double check the `test/cli/agent_cli_connection_retry_test.dart` pinning (already passed in the cli run).

One more thing to verify — the flutter_app host: PR description says "The flutter app host gets the attempt-budget bound only (null deadline seam default)". My changes don't touch the deadline seam. flutter_app doesn't use transientRetryStreamFunction? It might wrap streams too — but my changes are behavior-preserving for pure transport chains and the notice signature is unchanged. The flutter_app test suite is separate (`cd flutter_app && flutter test`) — the fast gate runs it only for flutter_app/packages paths. My changes are lib/ + test/ only → the per-PR gate is `dart test --exclude-tags integration` (running).

Now write response.md.

